<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ju County</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Juxian</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ju County, or Juxian, is a county in Rizhao, in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shandong">Shandong</a> province, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. It occupies the site of Ju, capital of the State of Ju, a non-Zhou state of the Dongyi peoples conquered by Chu in 431 BCE. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neolithic">Neolithic</a> sites in the county have yielded pottery bearing some of the earliest marks discussed as precursors of Chinese writing.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ju-county.jpg" alt="Ju County" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sprt98 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E8%8E%92%E5%9B%BD%E5%8F%A4%E5%9F%8E%E2%80%94%E2%80%94%E8%8E%92%E5%B7%9E%E5%A4%A7%E8%A1%9702.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
